ns or whatever you can have  pretty radical shifts  in price regulation and the types of  shareholders that will invest massively  in infrastructure are very unhappy with  that  and so  we believe that in order for  this model to work  you would also need to look at  asset-based regulation the way for  example that water and electricity are  currently regulated where what is capped  is not the price it's the amount of  profit that the operation can do and  that creates a virtual circle because  excess profit has to be reinvested which  means more infrastructure so it creates  this kind of dynamic where  deploying more infrastructure is an  integral part of the business model it's  not anything new in a sense so are you  confident it might happen  what do you think what do you think it  will take for people to look at this  business model  i think  first of all  policymakers need to understand  that they have been  they haven't been subsidizing more  broadband they've been subsidizing  companies that are not  well suited to deploy infrastructure so  that they could deploy infrastructure so  they have to understand that and they  have to understand  that it's a market structure issue  more than an inherent issue of fiber  fiber in and of itself is not expensive  because expensive  is  a definition of  you know a private market player saying  well this is too much and i can't do it  but that depends on who the market  player is so first of all they have to  realize that and second they need a  certain amount of political courage to  say  well  sure  existing players are happy with the  market structure but it's not delivering  what we need for our country and so it  has to change now the good news is in in  some previous analysis we looked at  the impact of structural separation for  shareholders of telecom companies and  actually that impact is massively  positive so  we're just at the very beginning of this  whole education piece but we believe  that  all of the parties actually have only  positives  in this consideration it's just that  because it's a big shift it's going to  take some time  well let's hope we get there thanks very  much for joining us you're welcome
 

